From 7e8a25244e9605e60f712e236e84a7e580ecdd5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 22:44:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] (be) snapshot-remote-unwind populate PHDR cache at BE
 startup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Uncomment the existing updatePHDRCache() call in doris_main.cpp so the
lock-free dl_iterate_phdr override (patch 1) has a populated cache
before the coordinator runs libunwind remote against any captured
thread snapshot. The test runner (be/test/testutil/run_all_tests.cpp:109)
already calls updatePHDRCache() before RUN_ALL_TESTS, so this commit
only restores the production path.

In snapshot-remote-unwind the handler does NOT call libunwind — it
copies registers + bounded stack bytes into the slot and returns.
The COORDINATOR runs libunwind remote in a request thread, where
unw_step calls dl_iterate_phdr. The coordinator is not a signal
handler, so async-signal-safety is not the gate here; the jemalloc
heap-profile deadlock (libgcc backtracer reentering the loader against
the override) is, and the populated cache fixes it the same way.

The placement is the existing upstream-anchored line (between
`MemInfo::debug_string` and `BackendOptions::init`); the call must
precede `ExecEnv::init` because that line brings up the BE worker
pools whose threads can be captured as snapshot targets.

Reference: <ck>/programs/main.cpp:318.
---
 be/src/service/doris_main.cpp | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp b/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
index fd534bc77f0..fb7337a62fa 100644
--- a/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
+++ b/be/src/service/doris_main.cpp
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
 
 #include "cloud/cloud_backend_service.h"
 #include "cloud/config.h"
+#include "common/phdr_cache.h"
 #include "common/stack_trace.h"
 #include "runtime/memory/mem_tracker_limiter.h"
 #include "storage/tablet/tablet_schema_cache.h"
@@ -585,10 +586,21 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
     LOG(INFO) << doris::DiskInfo::debug_string();
     LOG(INFO) << doris::MemInfo::debug_string();
 
-    // PHDR speed up exception handling, but exceptions from dynamically loaded libraries (dlopen)
-    // will work only after additional call of this function.
-    // rewrites dl_iterate_phdr will cause Jemalloc to fail to run after enable profile. see #
-    // updatePHDRCache();
+    // Reason: populate the PHDR cache before any thread that may run the
+    // ck-phdr-unwind signal handler exists. Once `BackendOptions::init` +
+    // `ExecEnv::init` bring up the BE worker pools (next lines), a worker
+    // can enter the handler, which calls `unw_step` -> `dl_iterate_phdr`;
+    // without the populated cache the override falls through to the libc
+    // function and takes the loader lock, which is not async-signal-safe.
+    // Reason: jemalloc heap-profile previously crashed against the override
+    // because libgcc's backtracer reentered the loader. Profiling defaults
+    // to OFF in this round's test build, so the prebuilt jemalloc is safe;
+    // turning profiling on requires the jemalloc rebuild documented in the
+    // build-system patch + build-facts.md.
+    // Reference: <ck>/programs/main.cpp:318 (ClickHouse calls
+    // updatePHDRCache near the top of main; Doris keeps the existing
+    // upstream-anchored placement to avoid moving init order).
+    updatePHDRCache();
     if (!doris::BackendOptions::init()) {
         exit(-1);
     }
